<article class="env-lemma" id="0AG8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AG8">Lemma <span data-tag="0AG8">31.16.2</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $D \subset X$ be a closed subscheme corresponding to the quasi-coherent ideal sheaf $\mathcal{I} \subset \mathcal{O}_ X$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If for every $x \in D$ the ideal $\mathcal{I}_ x \subset \mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ can be generated by one element, then $D$ is locally principal. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If for every $x \in D$ the ideal $\mathcal{I}_ x \subset \mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ can be generated by a single nonzerodivisor, then $D$ is an effective Cartier divisor. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ be an affine neighbourhood of a point $x \in D$. Let $\mathfrak p \subset A$ be the prime corresponding to $x$. Let $I \subset A$ be the ideal defining the trace of $D$ on $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$. Since $A$ is Noetherian (as $X$ is locally Noetherian) the ideal $I$ is generated by finitely many elements, say $I = (f_1, \ldots , f_ r)$. Under the assumption of (1) we have $I_\mathfrak p = (f)$ for some $f \in A_\mathfrak p$. Then $f_ i = g_ i f$ for some $g_ i \in A_\mathfrak p$. Write $g_ i = a_ i/h_ i$ and $f = f'/h$ for some $a_ i, h_ i, f', h \in A$, $h_ i, h \not\in \mathfrak p$. Then $I_{h_1 \ldots h_ r h} \subset A_{h_1 \ldots h_ r h}$ is principal, because it is generated by $f'$. This proves (1). For (2) we may assume $I = (f)$. The assumption implies that the image of $f$ in $A_\mathfrak p$ is a nonzerodivisor. Then $f$ is a nonzerodivisor on a neighbourhood of $x$ by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/061L" data-tag="061L">10.68.6</a>. This proves (2). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>